                        <img src="data:image/png;base64,{img_discount_rating}" alt="Discount % vs Customer Rating">
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="insight-box">
                    <strong>Pricing Insight:</strong> The correlation between discount percentage and customer rating is <strong>{correlation_discount_rating:.3f}</strong>. This very weak/negative correlation implies that <strong>deeper discounts do not drive higher customer satisfaction</strong>. Discounts may temporarily increase sales velocity, but they do not offset poor product quality in reviews. Margin is likely being eroded unnecessarily on products that do not warrant deep promotions.
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- 4. Customer Engagement & Rating Distribution -->
            <div class="section" id="customer-engagement">
                <h2>Customer Engagement & Rating Distribution</h2>
                <p>Understanding the volume of ratings helps distinguish between niche, highly-rated items and mass-market products with proven track records.</p>

