                {top_products}
                <p><em>Common Positive Themes:</em> Value for money, reliable functionality, build quality, and accurate product descriptions.</p>

                <h3>Lowest Rated Products (Snapshot)</h3>
                {bottom_products}
                <p><em>Common Negative Themes:</em> Defective units, poor durability, mismatched expectations versus listing, and poor customer service/warranty support.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- 6. Strategic Recommendations -->
            <div class="section" id="recommendations">
                <h2>Strategic Recommendations</h2>
                <p>Based on the data analysis, we recommend the following strategic actions for category and product managers:</p>

                <ol class="recommendation-list">
                    <li>
                        <strong>Rationalize Discounting Strategies:</strong> 
                        With a correlation of {correlation_discount_rating:.3f} between discount percentage and ratings, we recommend dialing back aggressive discounting (which averages {avg_discount:.1f}% across the board). Focus promotional budgets on products that already have strong ratings (4.0+) to amplify conversion, rather than using discounts to salvage poorly rated inventory.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Address Bottom-Tier Categories:</strong> 
                        Categories appearing lower on the "Average Rating by Main Category" chart require an immediate catalog audit. Implement stricter quality controls or delist consistently underperforming products (sub-3.5 stars) to protect brand equity, as discounts do not improve customer perception here.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Leverage High-Engagement 'Hero' Products:</strong> 
                        Products with both a high rating (>4.2) and high engagement (review count > {median_rating_count:,.0f}) are the catalog's anchors. Increase visibility for these products through sponsored ads or bundle them with lower-visibility items to improve overall cart size, as they represent proven customer satisfaction.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Optimize Pricing Tiering:</strong>
                        Ensure product descriptions and images are highly accurate to prevent expectation mismatches, which drive the lowest ratings. The data shows that "value for money" drives positive sentiment more than absolute low price or high discount percent. Focus marketing copy on value and durability rather than just "percentage off."
                    </li>
                </ol>
            </div>

        </div>
    </body>
    </html>
    '''

